<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Final Exam Review: the slides of the two in-class review sessions.

  The deck is the instructor's own HTML file (math14-final-review-slides,
  Nov 2026), at assets/final-review-slides.html; it is served from the
  external directory and embedded here in an iframe, the way
  subsec-brain-map.ptx embeds the brain map, with a link to open it full
  size.  Two sessions of six problems each, every problem followed by its
  solution slides.

  This repository carries the full deck, with solutions.  The student
  skeletal site (MATH14-Skeletal) has a problems-only copy until the
  solutions are released; see the comment in its copy of this file.

  The "sec-exercises-" id prefix lets assets/unnumbered-chapter.css hide
  its number like the rest of the chapter.  Included at the end of the
  assignments chapter, after the Exam 3 Review Session.
-->
<section xml:id="sec-exercises-final-review-session" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Final Exam Review</title>

  <p>
    The slides of the final exam review, in two sessions of six problems
    each: Session 1 (Problems 1 to 6) on curves, line integrals and
    multiple integrals, and Session 2 (Problems 7 to 12) on applications
    and the big theorems.
  </p>
  <p>
    Try each problem before you look at its solution. In the slides, <q>Next</q> (or the right arrow key) moves on
    one slide or one step at a time, and <q>Read all</q> shows every slide
    on one scrolling page. For comfortable reading,
    <url href="external/final-review-slides.html" visual="">open the slides full size in a new tab</url>.
  </p>

  <interactive xml:id="interactive-final-review-slides" iframe="final-review-slides.html" width="100%" aspect="4:3">
    <instructions>
      <p>
        One problem per slide. <q>Next</q> and <q>Back</q> move through
        the slides; <q>Read all</q> stacks every slide on one page.
      </p>
    </instructions>
    <static>
      <p>Slides of the final exam review (view in the HTML version).</p>
    </static>
  </interactive>

</section>
